S|       17      EXT. SINGAPORE - DAY                                    17         
O|
N,G|               We drift over the magnificent high-rises of Singapore.             
O|
Y|               ON SCREEN:  SINGAPORE - 13h00                                      
O|
S|       18      INT. ARMS FAIR - SINGAPORE - AFTERNOON                  18         
O|
N|               A huge hall filled with a maze of stands showcasing MILITARY       
N|               HARDWARE: Missiles, machine guns, armored vehicles...              
N,M|               IBS (Integrated Battlefield Solutions) operate on Stand B59.       
O|
N|               FOUR COMPANY MANNEQUINS demonstrate military clothing. One         
N|               wears undergarments, the second fatigues and the third is in       
N|               full operational military body armour.                             
O|
N,I|               JAMES WILLETT, British Foreign Secretary, pale and sweaty in       
N|               the heat, stands in front of the company name and slogan -         
N|               Soldier Safety First - as he speaks to a small audience            
N|               gathered around the stand.                                         
O|
O|
O|                    YELLOW SHOOTING SCRIPT    12 September 2014    10.            
O|
C|                                   JAMES                                          
U|                         On behalf of the British                                 
U|                         government, I am proud to introduce                      
U|                         Integrated Battlefield Solutions, a                      
U|                         UK company leading the field in the                      
U|                         production of life-saving,                               
U|                         lightweight military clothing.                           
U|                         Protecting our soldiers in the                           
U|                         field of battle is at the core of                        
U|                         my government’s commitment to our                        
U|                         armed forces. Soldier safety first                       
U|                         is why we are in partnership.                            
N,I|               IBS director, NIGEL ADLER, beside him, nods vigorously.            
C,E|                                   JAMES (CONT’D)                                 
U|                         And so I am very pleased to                              
U|                         introduce you to IBS managing                            
U|                         director, Mister Nigel Adler.                            
O|
N|               A ripple of applause from the BRITISH REPS - but most of the       
N|               people watching are invited FOREIGN BUYERS and they wait in        
N|               silence for ADLER to speak.                                        
O|
N,I|               Also watching are KATE BARNES (25), PR to the Foreign              
N,I|               Secretary, and TOM BELLAMY (28), his aide.                         
C|                                   ADLER                                          
U|                         Thank you very much, Foreign                             
U|                         Secretary. We feel extremely                             
